<div style="margin: 2rem 0; padding: 2rem; background: var(--bg-secondary); border-radius: 4px;">
  <h3>About the World Map</h3>
  <p>
    The world map (M6) is a persistent database of rooms discovered by the agent during exploration.
    It tracks:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Room identity:</strong> Signature-based recognition (name + exits + description) to distinguish same-named rooms</li>
    <li><strong>Connections:</strong> Exit directions and their target rooms, with confidence levels (confirmed/probable/ambiguous)</li>
    <li><strong>Visits:</strong> How many times each room was visited, by which actor</li>
    <li><strong>Confidence:</strong> Rooms are probabilistically identified via reciprocity testing (moving back validates the edge)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>When is the world map created?</h3>
  <p>
    The world map is created during agent execution when:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>NavigationTracker is enabled and hooked into tool results</li>
    <li>The agent executes <code>look</code> or <code>move</code> commands</li>
    <li>MUD output is parsed and rooms are reconciled into <code>.boukensha/world.db</code></li>
  </ol>

  <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
    <strong>To see a world map:</strong> Run an agent with M6 (WorldDB) enabled for a session,
    then view this page again after exploration completes.
  </p>
</div>
